      <activity id="3bfede4d-d4e3-5d57-9fae-0508b399c14f" activityNameId="208e2b33-a0dd-5b2f-b1b7-e63ae9e15d8f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Cladding, crossbar-pole, aluminium, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Cladding, crossbar-pole, aluminium, at plant
The data is calculated per 1 m2 of cladding. The aluminium cladding weighs 86.7 kg per m2. Production and disposal of glazing updated based on QualiBob data. Philippe Stolz, September 2016.\nGeography: Data based on a recently built official building in Switzerland.\nTechnology: The technology represented in this dataset is mainly related to the production of the various parts integrated in the cladding construction.\nVersion: 2.2\nEnergy values: Undefined\nLocal category: Bauteile\nLocal subcategory: Fassade\nUVEK 2022 source file:07150.XML\n\n
UUID: 6d120328-1f3a-3061-af19-fe6dbb29514b
This dataset describes the processes and materials required to build 1m2 (visible area) of an aluminium cladding, type crossbar-pole. No transport activities between production and construction site are taken into account. 
Location: undefined
Technology: The technology represented in this dataset is mainly related to the production of the various parts integrated in the cladding construction.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Company documentation 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: The assumption that this single Swiss dataset is representative for the whole Europe is taken into account in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6d120328-1f3a-3061-af19-fe6dbb29514b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
